<!--
Scenario 10 - FALSE NEGATIVE: fast main-lane car (120 km/h) beyond ENTRY_ZONE_M=100 m

The merging car departs near the end of the entering ramp (departPos=43, leaving
only 20.4 m to the merge) so the detection trigger fires almost immediately (t~0).
At that moment the highway car is 140 m from the merge — just beyond ENTRY_ZONE_M
(100 m) — so the detector skips it.

At 120 km/h (33.3 m/s) the highway car reaches the merge in ~4.2 s.  The merging
car is still on the ramp.  This is a real collision risk that goes undetected.

Expected (ground truth): unsafe
Detector output:         safe  (false negative - ENTRY_ZONE_M too short)
Fix:                     increase ENTRY_ZONE_M from 100 m to at least 150 m

Note: the kinematic fallback cannot reproduce this false negative because the
entering.json route (73.4 m) causes the trigger to fire after 3.2 s, by which
time the highway car has closed to ~33 m (inside the zone).  SUMO is required
to reproduce this scenario correctly.
-->
<routes>
    <vType id="car" accel="2.6" decel="4.5" sigma="0.0" length="4.5"
           maxSpeed="40.0" minGap="2.5"/>

    <!-- Merging car starts 20.4 m from merge (43 m along the 63.4 m edge)
         so the trigger fires at t~0.  -->
    <vehicle id="merging_car" type="car" depart="0.0"
             departLane="0" departPos="43" departSpeed="16.67">
        <route edges="entering highway_out"/>
    </vehicle>

    <!-- 140 m before merge: 182.5 - 140 = 42.5 -->
    <vehicle id="main_car" type="car" depart="0.0"
             departLane="0" departPos="42.5" departSpeed="33.33">
        <route edges="highway_in highway_out"/>
    </vehicle>
</routes>
